===Etymology 2===
1780, from {{der|en|non|hrukka||wrinkle, crease}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*hrunkijō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*hrunkitō||fold, wrinkle}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to turn, bend}}. Akin to {{cog|is|hrukka||wrinkle, crease, ruck}}, {{cog|goh|runza||fold, wrinkle, crease}}, {{cog|de|Runzel||wrinkle}}, {{cog|dum|ronse||frown}}. More at {{l|en|frounce}}. Possibly related to {{cog|ga|roc}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|to crease or fold (something)}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To crease or fold.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1956|author=w:C. S. Lewis|title=w:The Last Battle|publisher=Collins, 1998|section=Chapter 8|text=Puzzle begged very hard to have the lion-skin taken off him. He said it was too hot and the way it was '''rucked''' up on his back was uncomfortable {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1959|author=w:Peter De Vries|title=The Tents of Wickedness|page=28|text="What, exactly, happened down cellar?" Appleyard asked, straightening with his heel a '''rucked''' rug.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1989|author=w:Carol Shields|chapter=Block Out|title=The Collected Stories|publisher=Random House Canada, 2004|page=299|text=She wore long dangling earrings faced with mirrors, and white [[Bermuda shorts]] '''rucked''' back to reveal knees and thighs like [[waxed]] maple.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=w:Nadine Gordimer|chapter=L,U, C, I, E.|title=Loot and Other Stories|location=New York|publisher=Farrar, Straus & Giroux|text=The army had a shooting range up there hidden in the chestnut forests, that was all; like a passing plane '''rucking''' the fabric of perfect silence, the shots brought all that shatters continuity in life, the violence of emotions, the trajectories of demands and contests of will.}}
# {{senseid|en|to become creased or folded}} {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become creased or folded.
#* {{RQ:Wharton Summer|chapter=XII|page=178|passage="Will you come over now and try on your dress?" Ally asked, looking at her with wistful admiration. "I want to be sure the sleeves don't '''ruck''' up the same as they did yesterday."}}

